# Meta Pixel id for heybinder.com, from Events Manager.
#
# Everything in src/lib/analytics no-ops while this is empty, so a local run and
# a preview build send nothing. Set it in the Netlify build environment for
# production only. It is a public identifier, visible in the page source — the
# Conversions API token, which is a secret, lives in binderr_be and never here.
VITE_META_PIXEL_ID=

# Branch link that stands in front of the app stores, so a download carries the
# campaign token through the install (Phase 2 — the mobile funnel).
#
# Empty is the normal state: the store buttons then point straight at the App
# Store and Play Store, which is what they did before Phase 2. Set it in the
# Netlify build environment only. Vite inlines it at build time, so changing it
# needs a REBUILD, not a redeploy of the same artefact.
#
# The Branch link's own $desktop_url must be set to the web app — Branch routes
# by user agent, and a desktop visitor otherwise reaches a Branch error page.
VITE_BRANCH_DOWNLOAD_URL=
